From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pyproject: widen license-files to cover bundled libraries

`license-files = ["LICENSE.md"]` is an explicit PEP 639 list, so it has
no default glob behind it: a `LICENSE.<dep>` dropped at the project root
for a library compiled into the wheel is silently ignored. The wheel
ships libSDL2 (zlib) next to the extension, and `_ale_py` statically
links OpenCV core/imgproc (Apache-2.0) and nanobind (BSD-3-Clause), yet
only ALE's own GPL-2.0 notice lands in dist-info/licenses. scikit-build-core
refuses the SKBUILD_WHEEL_LICENSE_FILES override while project.license-files
is set, so the list itself has to change.

`LICENSE*` still matches only LICENSE.md in a clean checkout, so the sdist
is unchanged; the staged `LICENSE.<dep>` files are picked up in the wheel.

Upstream's own wheels carry the same gap: only LICENSE.md ships in
dist-info/licenses, with no notice for the bundled SDL2 or the statically
linked OpenCV and nanobind.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against Farama-Foundation/Arcade-Learning-Environment]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 readme = "README.md"
 requires-python = ">=3.10"
 license = "GPL-2.0-only"
-license-files = ["LICENSE.md"]
+license-files = ["LICENSE*"]
 keywords = ["reinforcement-learning", "arcade-learning-environment", "atari"]
 authors = [
     {name = "Marc G. Bellemare"},
--
